# Full d39 figure scene, set up for hand positioning.
#
# Everything is already applied: models, superposition, colours, side chains,
# Arg18, dashed distances and every label. All that is left to do by hand is
# rotate the structure and drag the labels.
#
# ONE LABEL PER RESIDUE. ChimeraX allows a single label per residue, so an atom
# label and a residue label on the same residue, or two atom labels on it,
# overwrite each other. The three distance values are therefore anchored on
# NEIGHBOURING residues that carry no name of their own:
#
#   "2.97 A"  on residue 44, next to Asp45      (d39_s0)
#   "2.68 A"  on residue 40, next to Arg39      (d39_s0)
#   "3.43 A"  on residue 44, next to Val36      (d39_s1)
#
# d39_s1 names Val36, the partner in its one remaining contact, plus Thr45 and
# Lys39, the residues that replaced d39_s0's Asp45 and Arg39 and so removed the
# other two contacts.
#
# They start next to the wrong side chain on purpose. Drag them onto their
# dashed lines.
#
# HOW TO USE
#   right-click drag             moves a label (mode is set below)
#   left-click drag              rotates
#   hide #2 models / show #3 models    switch to the other design
#   label #2/A:18@CB height 0.5        resize one label, keeps its position
#
# WHEN DONE
#   save positioned.cxs
# in this folder, then say so. The session stores the camera and every label
# offset, and the final panels are rendered from it by capture_positioned.cxc,
# so nothing has to be redone by hand.

close session

open data/wt_pikp1_avrpikf.pdb
open data/d39_s0_coldstart_s2.pdb
open data/d39_s1_coldstart_s1.pdb
rename #1 wt
rename #2 d39_s0
rename #3 d39_s1

windowsize 1600 1200
dssp
hide atoms
show cartoon
set bgColor white
lighting flat
graphics silhouettes true width 1.5

# Superpose both designs on the wild-type receptor, then hide the effectors.
matchmaker #2/A to #1/A
matchmaker #3/A to #1/A
hide /B cartoon
hide /B atoms

# Shared palette with render_wt_vs_design5.cxc.
color cornflower blue
color #1/A:33-45 red
color #2/A:33-48 red
color #3/A:33-48 red
color #1/A:73-78 purple
color #2/A:76-81 purple
color #3/A:76-81 purple
color #1/A:14-26 tan
color #2/A:14-26 tan
color #3/A:14-26 tan

# The six design region 1 positions that differ between the two sequences.
# Side chain atoms only, so the cartoon stays design-region red.
show #2/A:36,39,40,44,45,46 atoms
show #3/A:36,39,40,44,45,46 atoms
style #2/A:36,39,40,44,45,46 stick
style #3/A:36,39,40,44,45,46 stick
size #2/A:36,39,40,44,45,46 stickRadius 0.15
size #3/A:36,39,40,44,45,46 stickRadius 0.15
color #2/A:36,39,40,44,45,46 & sidechain dark slate gray target a
color #3/A:36,39,40,44,45,46 & sidechain dark slate gray target a
color #2/A:36,39,40,44,45,46 & sidechain byhetero target a
color #3/A:36,39,40,44,45,46 & sidechain byhetero target a

# Arg18, the one helix A residue whose contact with the loop differs.
show #2/A:18 atoms
show #3/A:18 atoms
style #2/A:18 stick
style #3/A:18 stick
size #2/A:18 stickRadius 0.15
size #3/A:18 stickRadius 0.15
color #2/A:18 & sidechain tan target a
color #3/A:18 & sidechain tan target a
color #2/A:18 & sidechain byhetero target a
color #3/A:18 & sidechain byhetero target a

hide H

# Dashed contacts. d39_s0 keeps a salt bridge to Asp45 and a guanidinium pair
# with Arg39; in d39_s1 both partners are substituted away and only a van der
# Waals approach to the Val36 methyl is left.
~distance
distance #2/A:18@NE #2/A:45@OD2
distance #2/A:18@NH2 #2/A:39@NH2
distance #3/A:18@NE #3/A:36@CG2
distance style color black dashes 8 radius 0.05 decimalPlaces 2
label delete pseudobonds

# Residue names, one per residue.
label #2/A:18 residues text "Arg18" height 0.7 color black
label #2/A:39 residues text "Arg39" height 0.7 color black
label #2/A:45 residues text "Asp45" height 0.7 color black
label #3/A:18 residues text "Arg18" height 0.7 color black
label #3/A:39 residues text "Lys39" height 0.7 color black
label #3/A:45 residues text "Thr45" height 0.7 color black

# Distance values, on neighbouring residues that carry no name.
label #2/A:44 residues text "2.97 A" height 0.7 color black
label #2/A:40 residues text "2.68 A" height 0.7 color black
label #3/A:36 residues text "Val36" height 0.7 color black
label #3/A:44 residues text "3.43 A" height 0.7 color black

view orient
turn x 225
turn y 345
turn z 45
turn y -30
turn x -10
view
zoom 1.15

# Right-click drags labels.
mousemode rightMode "move label"

hide #1 models
hide #3 models
show #2 models
